@meta
id: 04-10
title: Drawing a line with a count
chapter: 04
type: lesson
skills: count-prefix, hjkl
par: 28
minutes: 5
vscode: hold the hyphen key and count the characters by eye
open: payments.md

@brief
`Payments module` at the top of this document has an underline of `=` the
same length as the title. That is how the rest of the docs are written.

Two rules are missing, and both have to be the right length:

  1. Under the `Provider limits` heading, a new line of exactly fifteen
     hyphens — the heading is fifteen characters long.

  2. Under the `Everything below this line is generated...` sentence, a
     separator of exactly sixty-four hyphens.

Nobody counts hyphens by holding the key down. A count in front of an
insert command gives you an exact number of characters for the price of
typing the number.

@keys
| `15i-` `Esc` | insert fifteen hyphens |
| `o` | open a line below and insert on it |
| `j` `k` | down, up |

@hints
`o` gets you a new empty line in the right place. Then you need to get
back out of insert mode before a count will mean anything, because in
insert mode a digit is just a digit.
--
From normal mode on the empty line: the count, then `i`, then the one
character you want repeated, then `Esc`.
--
`o` `Esc` puts you on a new empty line in normal mode. Then `15i-` and
`Esc`. Do the same lower down with `64i-`.

@solution
    7j o <Esc> 15i- <Esc>
    6j o <Esc> 64i- <Esc>
    :wq<Enter>

Twenty-two keystrokes for seventy-nine hyphens.

The `o` `Esc` pair is worth noticing on its own. `o` is how you make a
line; `Esc` immediately after is how you make an *empty* one and get back
to normal mode, where counts work. In insert mode, `15` is the characters
`1` and `5`.

You will reach for this more often than you expect: rules in markdown,
padding in a fixture, a column of eighty `#` in a shell script, forty
underscores in a test string. Any time you would have held a key down and
then counted what came out, the count is the answer. Holding a key down
is guesswork with a cleanup step.

@start payments.md
Payments module
===============

The module owns charges, refunds and the webhook that reconciles them.
It talks to exactly one provider and knows nothing about orders beyond
the id it is given.

Provider limits

  Charges per second        25
  Refund window             90 days
  Webhook retry attempts    6

Everything below this line is generated. Do not edit it by hand.

